  "notes": "USAGE:\nMore literary and refined than {妊娠|にんしん}する. Often encountered in novels, historical texts, and formal announcements. In everyday conversation, {妊娠|にんしん}する or the colloquial できる are more common.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {子|こ}を{身籠|みごも}る (to conceive a child)\n- {身籠|みごも}っている (to be pregnant)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {妊娠|にんしん}する: to become pregnant — the standard, neutral medical/everyday term\n- {懐妊|かいにん}する: to become pregnant — very formal, used for royalty or public figures",
